WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.476 --> 00:00:18.852
Is everyone all right?

2
00:00:18.936 --> 00:00:19.936
Where's Jimmy?

3
00:00:24.399 --> 00:00:27.819
Oh. man. this is gonna get everywhere.

4
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.447
Hey. uh...

5
00:00:31.782 --> 00:00:33.700
What are you wearing?

6
00:00:33.784 --> 00:00:35.619
Wait. what am I wearing?

7
00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.371
<i>Well met. champions.</i>

8
00:00:38.497 --> 00:00:40.415
<i>Let the contest begin.</i>

9
00:00:40.499 --> 00:00:41.750
-Contest?
-What was that?

10
00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:46.338
How are my favorite mortals?

11
00:00:46.421 --> 00:00:48.173
Mxy. what's going on?

12
00:00:48.257 --> 00:00:49.299
Oh!

13
00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:53.220
I'm getting divorced.

14
00:00:53.303 --> 00:00:54.303
What?

15
00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.475
Mxy. why are we here?

16
00:00:58.559 --> 00:00:59.935
You're cute when you're anxious.

17
00:01:00.018 --> 00:01:01.353
Glitzy!

18
00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:05.899
You called. my former darling?

19
00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:08.068
This is Ms. Gsptlsnz.

20
00:01:08.151 --> 00:01:09.361
You can call me Glitzy.

21
00:01:09.444 --> 00:01:10.862
My soon to be ex-wife.

22
00:01:10.946 --> 00:01:12.614
Charmed.

23
00:01:12.698 --> 00:01:14.866
-That answered nothing.
-You have a wife?

24
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.535
Ex-wife. Keep up!

25
00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:17.929
Glitzy and I are untying the knot.

26
00:01:17.953 --> 00:01:19.556
but instead of all that
courtroom business.

27
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:22.040
-our people settle things...
-With a contest?

28
00:01:22.124 --> 00:01:26.211
Yes. Super-brain. a contest.
tournament. games. whatever.

29
00:01:26.295 --> 00:01:29.131
Glitzy and I have each
recruited a team of players.

30
00:01:29.214 --> 00:01:30.549
You're my team.

31
00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:32.426
Gullible Superman. Jimmy Lamebird.

32
00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:35.762
Question Mark Kara. and Fun Lois.

33
00:01:35.846 --> 00:01:38.265
<i>The teams compete
in a series of challenges.</i>

34
00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:41.018
<i>Each challenge cleared gets you A. a key</i>

35
00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.478
<i>and B. entry to the next ring.</i>

36
00:01:43.562 --> 00:01:45.897
<i>Whoever's team collects the most keys</i>

37
00:01:45.981 --> 00:01:47.375
<i>and gets to the center ring fastest</i>

38
00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:48.609
<i>determines whether Glitzy or I</i>

39
00:01:48.692 --> 00:01:51.403
<i>get the house. speedboat.
Galaxy. etcetera!</i>

40
00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:53.989
What if we do not wish to be pawns?

41
00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:55.157
Right.

42
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.160
Almost forgot.

43
00:01:58.243 --> 00:02:01.913
Lose and you will never see
your precious universe again.

44
00:02:01.997 --> 00:02:03.624
Sorry. Anything else?

45
00:02:03.707 --> 00:02:05.876
-So we'd be trapped here?
-Forever.

46
00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.437
Do you think you will get away with this?

47
00:02:07.461 --> 00:02:10.088
If we're your team.
then who's Glitzy team?

48
00:02:10.172 --> 00:02:12.466
Yes. Yes. Ooh. yes.

49
00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:13.550
And don't worry about it.

50
00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.886
We have Superman.

51
00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:18.347
We... we don't have Superman.

52
00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:19.765
What's that?

53
00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:21.433
I lost my powers.

54
00:02:21.516 --> 00:02:23.769
You lost your...

55
00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:25.228
powers?

56
00:02:25.312 --> 00:02:26.521
Before my divorce?

57
00:02:26.605 --> 00:02:29.024
I needed Superman.

58
00:02:29.107 --> 00:02:32.444
Clark Kent is useless to me.

59
00:02:34.321 --> 00:02:35.947
Embarrassing.

60
00:02:36.031 --> 00:02:41.244
Anyway. it's my great pleasure
to introduce Team Glitzy.

61
00:02:43.038 --> 00:02:45.332
First up. General Lane.

62
00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:46.333
Oh. no.

63
00:02:46.416 --> 00:02:49.127
That is. General Lois Lane.

64
00:02:49.211 --> 00:02:50.587
Oh. no.

65
00:02:50.671 --> 00:02:52.130
Good Lex Luthor...

66
00:02:54.591 --> 00:02:59.179
Scion Kara from the House of El.

67
00:02:59.262 --> 00:03:01.223
And Flamebird Jimmy.

68
00:03:01.306 --> 00:03:03.058
Oh. that's just me.

69
00:03:03.141 --> 00:03:04.434
Flamebird.

70
00:03:11.066 --> 00:03:14.111
Nope. A way cooler me.

71
00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:15.654
Hey. Hi. excuse me.

72
00:03:15.737 --> 00:03:16.863
I was swindled.

73
00:03:16.947 --> 00:03:18.323
I chose Superman.

74
00:03:18.407 --> 00:03:19.991
Instead. I got a bumbling. useless.

75
00:03:20.075 --> 00:03:21.576
nearsighted reporter!

76
00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.494
Okay. man...

77
00:03:22.577 --> 00:03:24.871
The playing field must be leveled.

78
00:03:24.955 --> 00:03:27.082
How about no flying allowed?

79
00:03:27.165 --> 00:03:30.293
No. Buyer beware. your fault.

80
00:03:30.377 --> 00:03:32.295
Ruling. please.

81
00:03:32.379 --> 00:03:34.756
<i>The champions shall not fly.</i>

82
00:03:37.384 --> 00:03:39.970
Eat that. love of my life.

83
00:03:40.804 --> 00:03:41.722
What's happening?

84
00:03:41.805 --> 00:03:43.890
Mxy. I will crush him.

85
00:03:48.645 --> 00:03:50.814
When the big boy says "go."
cross the bridge.

86
00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:53.650
get the key. do it faster than them...

87
00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:55.402
and watch your step.

88
00:03:55.485 --> 00:03:58.113
<i>Let the first challenge commence.</i>

89
00:04:17.549 --> 00:04:18.800
Can you believe the way Glitzy

90
00:04:18.884 --> 00:04:22.554
is trying to get under my skin.
pitting me against her?

91
00:04:23.638 --> 00:04:25.766
It's not like that could ever be me.

92
00:04:25.849 --> 00:04:26.975
Right?

93
00:04:29.561 --> 00:04:30.561
Clark!

94
00:04:38.028 --> 00:04:39.154
Run!

95
00:04:46.787 --> 00:04:49.080
I'm sorry I wasn't fast enough.

96
00:04:49.164 --> 00:04:50.290
-I just...
-Is that...

97
00:04:52.042 --> 00:04:53.043
A key!

98
00:04:56.755 --> 00:04:58.298
I'll take that.

99
00:04:58.381 --> 00:05:00.675
How about a "thank you. team"?

100
00:05:00.759 --> 00:05:02.427
That would imply you did a good job.

101
00:05:02.511 --> 00:05:04.137
Hey. we got the key. didn't we?

102
00:05:04.221 --> 00:05:06.473
Just barely. Look at them.

103
00:05:11.603 --> 00:05:12.979
So? It's a tie.

104
00:05:13.063 --> 00:05:14.940
A tie? Pathetic!

105
00:05:15.023 --> 00:05:16.149
You didn't come here to tie.

106
00:05:16.233 --> 00:05:17.984
You came here to win!

107
00:05:18.068 --> 00:05:19.736
Next game.

108
00:05:26.284 --> 00:05:27.410
You.

109
00:05:27.494 --> 00:05:31.248
Ladies and ladies. may I present

110
00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:35.043
S'ivaan Mountain.

111
00:05:35.126 --> 00:05:37.504
Your mission.
should you choose to accept it...

112
00:05:37.587 --> 00:05:39.881
Ha! I jest. You don't have rights.

113
00:05:39.965 --> 00:05:43.260
Is to climb S'ivaan Mountain.

114
00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:44.553
Whoever gets to the top first

115
00:05:44.636 --> 00:05:46.847
wins this round's one and only key.

116
00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:49.307
As you ascend. the mountain will sink

117
00:05:49.391 --> 00:05:51.810
into the Manticore trench.

118
00:05:51.893 --> 00:05:53.162
Anyway. if you're too slow or slip.

119
00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:54.226
you'll meet the Manticore.

120
00:05:54.271 --> 00:05:57.065
Last team to make it to the top loses.

121
00:06:00.902 --> 00:06:02.821
This is the boy challenge.

122
00:06:02.904 --> 00:06:04.406
These are portal pieces.

123
00:06:04.489 --> 00:06:07.367
Find them. put them together.
make a portal. leave it.

124
00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:09.119
Whoever does it first wins.

125
00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:12.747
-That's it?
-Yes! Just win.

126
00:06:12.831 --> 00:06:13.831
Man!

127
00:06:16.459 --> 00:06:18.670
The mountain does not feel
like it is sinking.

128
00:06:18.753 --> 00:06:20.463
This is unchallenging.

129
00:06:20.547 --> 00:06:24.175
Yep. very unchallenging.

130
00:06:24.259 --> 00:06:28.013
Lois Lane. is it my fate
to become like... that?

131
00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:30.682
Her?

132
00:06:30.765 --> 00:06:32.392
I mean. you were like that.

133
00:06:32.475 --> 00:06:34.895
Look. I've met a whole league of Lois-es.

134
00:06:34.978 --> 00:06:37.022
These other selves mean nothing.

135
00:06:37.105 --> 00:06:38.982
Oh. now it is sinking.

136
00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:40.275
Go. go. go!

137
00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:45.697
Get to the top.

138
00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:47.240
Only one of us needs to win.

139
00:06:51.119 --> 00:06:52.120
Are you crazy?

140
00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.339
Do you think our Lois-es are okay?

141
00:07:03.798 --> 00:07:04.841
Whoa!

142
00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:14.017
You must be cautious. Other Kara.

143
00:07:23.151 --> 00:07:24.569
Okay. let's move.

144
00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:28.823
Shouldn't we hide out somewhere?

145
00:07:28.907 --> 00:07:30.492
I'm finding a way out.

146
00:07:30.575 --> 00:07:31.993
We can barely see.

147
00:07:32.077 --> 00:07:35.372
We don't know the area.
and there's a beast trying to hunt us.

148
00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:37.207
Lanes are doers. not complainers.

149
00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.500
I'm not complaining.

150
00:07:38.583 --> 00:07:40.377
But maybe we should wait where we fell in.

151
00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:41.878
What if our Karas need us?

152
00:07:41.962 --> 00:07:43.630
If they join us. they failed.

153
00:07:43.713 --> 00:07:45.632
They can handle the consequences.

154
00:07:45.715 --> 00:07:48.093
Wow. we are so different.

155
00:07:48.176 --> 00:07:51.388
Hmm. let me guess...
Mom died. Dad was distant.

156
00:07:51.471 --> 00:07:53.264
All you wanted was work. work. work.

157
00:07:53.348 --> 00:07:56.226
But instead you find
the "super man" of your dreams.

158
00:07:56.309 --> 00:07:59.604
learn the meaning of friendship.
and have a real swell time.

159
00:07:59.688 --> 00:08:01.231
That was me too.

160
00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:04.693
But then Clark lost his powers
and... and then his life.

161
00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:06.987
So go ahead and judge me.

162
00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:09.990
but the line between us isn't
as thick as you think it is.

163
00:08:13.827 --> 00:08:14.953
Ah!

164
00:08:24.796 --> 00:08:25.796
Ah!

165
00:08:26.798 --> 00:08:27.798
Why?

166
00:08:28.883 --> 00:08:30.885
No!

167
00:08:30.969 --> 00:08:31.969
Kara!

168
00:08:40.311 --> 00:08:41.563
You cheated.

169
00:08:41.646 --> 00:08:43.898
No. I won.

170
00:08:43.982 --> 00:08:46.317
You had the chance to do the same.

171
00:08:46.401 --> 00:08:47.944
and you wanted to.

172
00:08:48.028 --> 00:08:50.447
Do not lie to yourself. Kara.

173
00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:52.407
This is who we are.

174
00:08:59.122 --> 00:09:00.415
Aha!

175
00:09:01.583 --> 00:09:04.085
Check it out. Clark... and others.

176
00:09:04.169 --> 00:09:06.004
One more down. one more to...

177
00:09:06.087 --> 00:09:07.630
-Hey!
-It's ours.

178
00:09:07.714 --> 00:09:08.840
It's clearly orange.

179
00:09:08.923 --> 00:09:10.550
It's hard to tell.

180
00:09:10.633 --> 00:09:12.093
Anyone could have made that mistake.

181
00:09:12.177 --> 00:09:15.513
I wonder how many of our pieces
you may have stolen by mistake.

182
00:09:15.597 --> 00:09:17.974
-Look. I don't think...
-Are you saying I'm lying?

183
00:09:18.058 --> 00:09:20.852
I'm suggesting
there may be foul play. yes.

184
00:09:20.935 --> 00:09:21.936
Hey. let's not...

185
00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:24.522
You'd only think like that
if you were doing it yourself.

186
00:09:24.606 --> 00:09:27.317
Okay. Lex. it was an honest mistake.

187
00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.027
but to make everyone feel better.

188
00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:30.862
why don't I look for pieces with you?

189
00:09:30.945 --> 00:09:33.823
And Jimmy. you can go with... Jimmy.

190
00:09:33.907 --> 00:09:36.659
So we can all be sure
everyone's playing fair.

191
00:09:36.743 --> 00:09:37.786
Deal?

192
00:09:37.869 --> 00:09:39.079
-Very well.
-Fine.

193
00:09:39.162 --> 00:09:41.706
All right. Jimmy time! Let's go.

194
00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:43.124
Just be cool. man.

195
00:09:47.128 --> 00:09:50.673
So your world seems like a...
interesting place.

196
00:09:50.757 --> 00:09:52.175
How'd you all end up together?

197
00:09:52.258 --> 00:09:53.968
No more Superman.

198
00:09:54.052 --> 00:09:54.928
This one's yours.

199
00:09:55.011 --> 00:09:56.763
What? Oh. uh. thank you.

200
00:09:56.846 --> 00:09:59.516
What happened to Superman in your world?

201
00:09:59.599 --> 00:10:01.309
Mistakes were made.

202
00:10:01.392 --> 00:10:03.311
I made a mistake.

203
00:10:03.394 --> 00:10:05.897
And with Superman gone.
we didn't stand a chance

204
00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:07.107
when the hunger dogs came.

205
00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:08.608
Everything changed for the worse.

206
00:10:08.691 --> 00:10:10.527
And we did what we had to.

207
00:10:11.611 --> 00:10:13.029
Are you helping or what?

208
00:10:13.113 --> 00:10:14.113
Right. right.

209
00:10:16.783 --> 00:10:19.035
Okay. that suit is awesome.

210
00:10:19.119 --> 00:10:20.120
I know. right?

211
00:10:20.203 --> 00:10:23.206
Kara and Lois can be
so negative sometimes.

212
00:10:23.289 --> 00:10:25.333
But. hey. if the hunger dogs
hadn't invaded.

213
00:10:25.416 --> 00:10:27.127
I wouldn't have this sick suit.

214
00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:30.505
-Uh. the what invaded?
-Always silver linings.

215
00:10:30.588 --> 00:10:32.632
Sick suit. Lex is good now.

216
00:10:32.715 --> 00:10:34.968
and we're all as close
as we were before Clark died.

217
00:10:35.051 --> 00:10:36.594
Clark died?

218
00:10:36.678 --> 00:10:38.805
Yep. just three best friends.

219
00:10:38.888 --> 00:10:40.890
We're all doing great.

220
00:10:40.974 --> 00:10:42.100
That doesn't sound great.

221
00:10:42.183 --> 00:10:44.769
Everything is exactly the same.

222
00:10:44.853 --> 00:10:46.813
Well. except...

223
00:10:48.857 --> 00:10:51.526
I'm a superhero now! Pew. pew. Pew.

224
00:10:51.609 --> 00:10:52.837
-Right. Right.
-Pew. pew. pew. pew.

225
00:10:52.861 --> 00:10:54.696
But aren't you upset or worried about...

226
00:10:54.779 --> 00:10:56.156
Boo! Boo-hoo!

227
00:10:56.239 --> 00:10:58.867
Working together. Feelings?

228
00:10:59.909 --> 00:11:01.119
This is boring.

229
00:11:01.202 --> 00:11:03.079
The girls are done already.

230
00:11:03.913 --> 00:11:06.833
Release the Hell Hippos.

231
00:11:06.916 --> 00:11:08.293
The what?

232
00:11:15.758 --> 00:11:17.135
Do you have the last piece?

233
00:11:17.218 --> 00:11:18.845
No. do you?

234
00:11:18.928 --> 00:11:20.096
Looking for this?

235
00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:21.598
Oh. Yeah.

236
00:11:21.681 --> 00:11:22.974
There's only one.

237
00:11:23.057 --> 00:11:23.933
Give it to us.

238
00:11:24.017 --> 00:11:25.476
We're on your team.

239
00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:26.936
Team-shmeam.

240
00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:29.355
It's more fun watching you scream.

241
00:11:35.069 --> 00:11:37.113
Jimmy. give Lex the piece.

242
00:11:37.197 --> 00:11:38.198
What? No.

243
00:11:38.281 --> 00:11:39.908
Jimmy. I'm not Superman.

244
00:11:39.991 --> 00:11:42.702
I... give it to him or you'll all die!

245
00:11:52.295 --> 00:11:53.295
No.

246
00:11:54.714 --> 00:11:56.382
I'm so sorry. Jimmy. I...

247
00:11:59.177 --> 00:12:00.637
Clark.

248
00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:01.947
-Are you guys okay?
-What happened to you?

249
00:12:01.971 --> 00:12:03.139
We almost died.

250
00:12:03.223 --> 00:12:04.557
Yeah. I know. Us. too.

251
00:12:04.641 --> 00:12:06.517
Oh. you're fine. Grow up.

252
00:12:06.601 --> 00:12:08.770
Also. you're losing. losers!

253
00:12:08.853 --> 00:12:11.064
And another one for Glitzy.

254
00:12:12.357 --> 00:12:14.859
Good work.

255
00:12:14.943 --> 00:12:18.488
Do you people even want a universe?

256
00:12:18.571 --> 00:12:19.948
Mmm. could be worse.

257
00:12:20.031 --> 00:12:22.242
At least he didn't let
the Hell Hippos get us.

258
00:12:22.325 --> 00:12:24.244
Hell Hippos? Wait!

259
00:12:24.327 --> 00:12:27.789
Glitzy also got us away
before the Manticore attacked.

260
00:12:27.872 --> 00:12:29.374
Why are they saving us?

261
00:12:35.546 --> 00:12:37.173
Okay. dummies.

262
00:12:37.257 --> 00:12:38.925
This is a maze.

263
00:12:39.008 --> 00:12:40.051
All you gotta do this time

264
00:12:40.134 --> 00:12:42.887
is choose your one true path
and follow it.

265
00:12:42.971 --> 00:12:45.431
And how do we know which path is right?

266
00:12:45.515 --> 00:12:46.808
Pick the path you like best.

267
00:12:46.891 --> 00:12:49.185
Just don't let the trail go cold.

268
00:12:50.395 --> 00:12:51.938
Okay. bye.

269
00:12:52.021 --> 00:12:54.315
One day. I will crush him.

270
00:12:55.483 --> 00:12:56.526
Humanely.

271
00:12:59.612 --> 00:13:00.822
-Ah!
-Ah!

272
00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:04.909
Clark!

273
00:13:04.993 --> 00:13:06.286
Lois.

274
00:13:19.841 --> 00:13:20.841
Lois.

275
00:13:22.677 --> 00:13:23.677
What?

276
00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:35.481
I used to be Superman.

277
00:13:37.358 --> 00:13:38.484
Who am I now?

278
00:13:46.492 --> 00:13:48.494
Are you still my path?

279
00:14:00.173 --> 00:14:03.259
Great. more Lois-es?

280
00:14:03.343 --> 00:14:04.344
Nope.

281
00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:06.470
Nah.

282
00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:08.680
No.

283
00:14:10.099 --> 00:14:13.353
Not seeing any "one true paths" in here.

284
00:14:16.898 --> 00:14:18.149
I remember this.

285
00:14:21.235 --> 00:14:22.570
No.

286
00:14:22.653 --> 00:14:24.280
No. it can't...

287
00:14:25.907 --> 00:14:26.908
No.

288
00:14:30.161 --> 00:14:31.454
This can't be real.

289
00:14:33.164 --> 00:14:33.998
This...

290
00:14:34.082 --> 00:14:35.583
can't be...

291
00:14:39.462 --> 00:14:41.798
I. uh. talked to Flamebird Jimmy.

292
00:14:41.881 --> 00:14:43.966
He's pretending that everything's okay.

293
00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:45.134
that it'll all work out

294
00:14:45.218 --> 00:14:47.178
when it's falling apart in front of him.

295
00:14:48.137 --> 00:14:51.140
Perhaps that is our only path.

296
00:14:51.224 --> 00:14:54.894
No. look. I haven't been
a good friend. Kara.

297
00:14:54.977 --> 00:14:57.146
I haven't been a good anything.

298
00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:58.564
I still think you deserve better.

299
00:14:58.648 --> 00:15:01.401
So I am going to be better.

300
00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:03.694
I need to change.

301
00:15:06.239 --> 00:15:07.073
Say that again.

302
00:15:07.156 --> 00:15:08.825
Oh. that I need to change.

303
00:15:08.908 --> 00:15:10.368
And I... I mean it. Kara.

304
00:15:10.451 --> 00:15:12.912
-I know...
-Hush. That is it.

305
00:15:12.995 --> 00:15:14.455
When I saw Scion Kara.

306
00:15:14.539 --> 00:15:16.833
I feared that brainiac was right about me.

307
00:15:16.916 --> 00:15:19.627
that my one true self was like him.

308
00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:22.296
But I am not one thing.

309
00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:24.465
We are all creatures of change.

310
00:15:24.549 --> 00:15:26.676
We can become anything.

311
00:15:26.759 --> 00:15:27.677
Jimmy Flamebird.

312
00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:30.638
this game is a trick.

313
00:15:30.721 --> 00:15:34.517
We decide who we are every day.

314
00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:37.019
There is no one true path.

315
00:15:37.103 --> 00:15:39.689
The future is ours to shape.

316
00:15:46.988 --> 00:15:48.698
Wait. what happened?

317
00:15:48.781 --> 00:15:51.033
Anything can happen. Lois Lane.

318
00:15:51.117 --> 00:15:53.119
There is no one true path.

319
00:15:53.202 --> 00:15:54.263
That was the solution all...

320
00:15:54.287 --> 00:15:55.830
-Yea. real moving.
-Hey!

321
00:15:55.913 --> 00:15:57.290
What happened to the other team?

322
00:15:57.373 --> 00:15:58.916
Oh. them?

323
00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.377
One could say they missed the mark.

324
00:16:01.461 --> 00:16:03.463
Bunch of drips. huh!

325
00:16:03.546 --> 00:16:04.839
Total wash. Wait. wait!

326
00:16:04.922 --> 00:16:06.340
I got more.

327
00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:08.593
Not so fast.

328
00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:13.514
There's one game left.

329
00:16:15.266 --> 00:16:17.268
And Mama's gonna get that house.

330
00:16:24.192 --> 00:16:26.486
Aw. hamster balls.

331
00:16:26.569 --> 00:16:28.196
Can we keep them?

332
00:16:28.279 --> 00:16:29.947
You always do this.

333
00:16:30.031 --> 00:16:32.575
You get attached. they die. you're sad.

334
00:16:32.658 --> 00:16:35.077
My empathy makes me likable.

335
00:16:35.161 --> 00:16:37.788
First ball through
the obstacle course wins.

336
00:16:37.872 --> 00:16:40.333
-Ready. set...
-Wait!

337
00:16:40.416 --> 00:16:42.043
Things aren't adding up.

338
00:16:42.126 --> 00:16:42.960
She's right.

339
00:16:43.044 --> 00:16:44.271
For example. it hasn't seemed to matter

340
00:16:44.295 --> 00:16:46.923
-who wins the keys...
-As long as they're being won.

341
00:16:47.006 --> 00:16:50.051
Exactly.
Like. why did we both win the first game?

342
00:16:50.134 --> 00:16:51.886
And why do all the keys go
to the same place

343
00:16:51.969 --> 00:16:53.596
no matter who wins them?

344
00:16:53.679 --> 00:16:55.389
And who is that guy?

345
00:16:57.266 --> 00:17:00.561
Beings of your dimension
couldn't possibly understand...

346
00:17:00.645 --> 00:17:01.812
No...

347
00:17:01.896 --> 00:17:03.105
more...

348
00:17:03.189 --> 00:17:04.357
games!

349
00:17:05.107 --> 00:17:07.276
Very well. since you insist.

350
00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:10.696
That structure over there
is the cosmic anvil.

351
00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:13.366
A device that can reshape a universe.

352
00:17:13.449 --> 00:17:15.368
The keys unlock its power.

353
00:17:15.451 --> 00:17:16.571
We needed you lovely mortals

354
00:17:16.619 --> 00:17:18.788
to retrieve the keys because. well...

355
00:17:18.871 --> 00:17:20.164
There's a curse

356
00:17:20.248 --> 00:17:23.459
that prevents certain immortals
from unlocking it.

357
00:17:23.543 --> 00:17:26.212
-Okay? Happy now?
-No!

358
00:17:26.295 --> 00:17:27.775
That's why we've been doing all this?

359
00:17:30.383 --> 00:17:32.009
How about some incentive?

360
00:17:32.093 --> 00:17:34.679
The winners get to reshape their universe

361
00:17:34.762 --> 00:17:37.515
however they want!

362
00:17:37.598 --> 00:17:39.267
Fun Lois. lean in.

363
00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:41.435
You could pick whatever future you want.

364
00:17:41.519 --> 00:17:45.439
Clark. you could get your powers back.
Mm. mm?

365
00:17:45.523 --> 00:17:47.024
You could bring Clark back.

366
00:17:47.108 --> 00:17:48.484
Don't you mean Superman?

367
00:17:48.568 --> 00:17:49.402
No.

368
00:17:49.485 --> 00:17:52.822
Superman losing his powers was...
difficult.

369
00:17:52.905 --> 00:17:56.033
But when we lost Clark. we lost...
everything.

370
00:17:58.536 --> 00:18:00.997
Okay. let's play.

371
00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:02.540
Wait. guys. we... we...

372
00:18:02.623 --> 00:18:05.126
we can't just trust Mxy
to deliver on these promises.

373
00:18:05.209 --> 00:18:08.212
Maybe the reward is worth the risk.

374
00:18:08.296 --> 00:18:09.797
Well. what is the risk?

375
00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:11.299
What happens to the losers?

376
00:18:11.382 --> 00:18:15.970
The losers get turned into a gift
for my beloved wife.

377
00:18:16.053 --> 00:18:18.723
Maybe a Ficus. Huh.

378
00:18:18.806 --> 00:18:20.766
Beloved wife?

379
00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:22.685
Okay. you got us.

380
00:18:22.768 --> 00:18:25.438
This is a date. not a divorce.

381
00:18:25.521 --> 00:18:29.775
Just some good old fashioned role play
to spice things up.

382
00:18:29.859 --> 00:18:31.736
Oh. we do have fun.

383
00:18:33.237 --> 00:18:34.780
So what do you say?

384
00:18:34.864 --> 00:18:36.198
We can't play their game.

385
00:18:36.282 --> 00:18:38.159
Don't listen to Team Ficus.

386
00:18:38.242 --> 00:18:39.702
They're just afraid to lose.

387
00:18:39.785 --> 00:18:42.246
Look. I've dealt with Mxy before.

388
00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:43.473
and if he unlocks that thing.

389
00:18:43.497 --> 00:18:45.499
whatever he's gonna do with it
will not be good.

390
00:18:45.583 --> 00:18:47.710
What do you mean. "Dealt with him before"?

391
00:18:47.793 --> 00:18:51.339
Uh. what interest would
an immortal have in a reporter?

392
00:18:51.422 --> 00:18:52.423
No offense.

393
00:18:55.176 --> 00:18:56.969
What is. uh...

394
00:18:57.053 --> 00:18:58.262
I... I don't understand.

395
00:19:00.973 --> 00:19:01.974
It... it's...

396
00:19:02.058 --> 00:19:03.058
you.

397
00:19:03.809 --> 00:19:06.103
Did everyone know this but me?

398
00:19:06.187 --> 00:19:07.647
-Yes. hello.
-Yeah.

399
00:19:10.024 --> 00:19:12.610
I regret not listening to Superman when...

400
00:19:12.693 --> 00:19:14.070
When I had the chance.

401
00:19:14.153 --> 00:19:16.155
I'm not gonna make the same mistake twice.

402
00:19:20.576 --> 00:19:24.622
Hey. play now or I'll give you
something to regret.

403
00:19:25.748 --> 00:19:27.083
We aren't playing.

404
00:19:27.166 --> 00:19:31.295
Let me get this through your thick skulls!

405
00:19:31.379 --> 00:19:36.300
Defy me. and I will crush you
like the bugs you are.

406
00:19:36.384 --> 00:19:39.512
Play or die!

407
00:19:39.595 --> 00:19:41.597
Well. then we die.

408
00:19:41.681 --> 00:19:43.808
-Clark. what are you doing?
-Yeah. buddy.

409
00:19:43.891 --> 00:19:45.184
Go ahead. Mxy.

410
00:19:45.267 --> 00:19:47.645
There's nothing stopping you. right?

411
00:19:52.733 --> 00:19:57.697
<i>The hour has come
and the contest has no victor.</i>

412
00:19:57.780 --> 00:20:01.033
<i>My seal remains unbroken.</i>

413
00:20:01.117 --> 00:20:03.411
<i>Farewell. champions!</i>

414
00:20:03.494 --> 00:20:04.829
<i>Burn in hell. Mxy.</i>

415
00:20:04.912 --> 00:20:07.581
-Oh. no!
-No!

416
00:20:09.834 --> 00:20:11.210
I do not understand.

417
00:20:11.293 --> 00:20:13.212
Those were hourglasses...

418
00:20:13.295 --> 00:20:15.172
showing how much time
was left in the game.

419
00:20:15.256 --> 00:20:18.634
-And you knew it was game over.
-Game over.

420
00:20:18.718 --> 00:20:21.262
Not bad for a bumbling. useless.

421
00:20:21.345 --> 00:20:23.431
nearsighted reporter. huh. Mxy?

422
00:20:23.514 --> 00:20:26.517
No. my anvil!

423
00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:31.522
Why do you people always ruin everything?

424
00:20:31.605 --> 00:20:34.024
Why. why. why. why?

425
00:20:34.108 --> 00:20:36.736
Ugh. Oh. in front of the mortals?

426
00:20:36.819 --> 00:20:38.779
I can't watch this. I'm out.

427
00:20:38.863 --> 00:20:40.281
Glitzy. wait!

428
00:20:40.364 --> 00:20:41.741
It was just role play. baby.

429
00:20:41.824 --> 00:20:44.076
Baby. it was just role play.

430
00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:45.369
I...

431
00:20:45.453 --> 00:20:47.121
Hey. you never answered my question.

432
00:20:47.204 --> 00:20:48.372
Who is that guy?

433
00:20:50.082 --> 00:20:52.126
A sore loser.

434
00:20:54.044 --> 00:20:55.629
Whoa!

435
00:20:56.672 --> 00:20:59.175
Oh. my sweet tailored suit.

436
00:21:09.143 --> 00:21:11.562
Oh. Uh. hey. there. stranger.

437
00:21:12.563 --> 00:21:13.731
Fancy meeting you here.

438
00:21:13.814 --> 00:21:16.942
Yeah. I decided to wake up
a little earlier. clear my head.

439
00:21:17.026 --> 00:21:19.945
Same. I knew there was
a reason we were together.

440
00:21:20.029 --> 00:21:23.908
Yeah. I think. uh.
I actually feel better now than before.

441
00:21:23.991 --> 00:21:25.659
Whatever that was.

442
00:21:25.743 --> 00:21:28.954
I think I'm starting to like Clark Kent.

443
00:21:29.038 --> 00:21:30.456
Maybe he's enough.

444
00:21:30.539 --> 00:21:31.624
Of course he is.

445
00:21:34.335 --> 00:21:35.169
But how are you?

446
00:21:35.252 --> 00:21:38.130
I'm... kinda shaken. honestly.

447
00:21:38.214 --> 00:21:40.758
I thought I knew
what our future was gonna be.

448
00:21:40.841 --> 00:21:43.093
But now it feels like we can't keep up.

449
00:21:43.177 --> 00:21:46.764
Like we keep fighting
against these terrible futures.

450
00:21:46.847 --> 00:21:48.474
They're not terrible. Lois.

451
00:21:48.557 --> 00:21:49.892
They're just...

452
00:21:57.066 --> 00:21:58.317
Different.
